[{"text":"FCTraceFactor[expr] factors out all expressions inside a trace to which the trace doesn’t apply. For example, all objects that are not Dirac matrices can be safely factored out from every Dirac trace.","anchor":"fctracefactor"},{"text":"Overview, DiracTrace, SUNTrace.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"Pull constants out of the Dirac trace","anchor":"examples","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FCTraceFactor[DiracTrace[c1 . (c2*(GS[p1] + M)) . GA[\\[Mu]] . (c3*(GS[p2] + M2))]]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\text{c1} \\;\\text{c2} \\;\\text{c3} \\;\\text{tr}\\left(\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{\\text{p1}}+M\\right).\\bar{\\gamma }^{\\mu }.\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{\\text{p2}}+\\text{M2}\\right)\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Examples"}]